A few related remarks...

A change of floating eyes to some bright green (as done in variants?)
would be good.

It would probably be a good idea to use violet colour for *magic*
monsters (including MF/MMF, but for dwarf king that would then seem
inappropriate).
But the Nethack colours seems not to be intended for magic monsters,
rather used primarily for "lords", i.e. reflecting some social rank.

Offering the possibility to change ghosts from ' ' to something else,
say '8' (as so often seen), will provide more information than with
the default, in case that you are in an unexplored area and able to
ESP-detect monsters, since per default you will not see those ghosts
and shades. But with a visible glyph change you quickly detect bones
levels, and shades are no threat any more; this affects game play in
those situations significantly and is a Bad Thing, IMO.

